The public operation signatures are exact. Each body is the generator-owned C and JS import or a pure result adapter. Implementations do not ship as placeholder effects.

```python
def Instance.get_physical_device_image_format_properties(instance: Instance,
	physical: PhysicalDevice, query: ImageFormatQuery) -> IO(VkResult(ImageFormatProperties))
def Device.create_image(device: Device, info: ImageCreateInfo) -> IO(VkResult(Image))
def Device.destroy_image(device: Device, image: Image) -> IO(VkResult(Unit))
def Device.get_image_memory_requirements(device: Device, image: Image) -> IO(VkResult(MemoryRequirements))
def Device.bind_image_memory(device: Device, image: Image,
	memory: DeviceMemory, offset: W.U64) -> IO(VkResult(Unit))
def Device.create_image_view(device: Device, info: ImageViewCreateInfo) -> IO(VkResult(ImageView))
def Device.destroy_image_view(device: Device, view: ImageView) -> IO(VkResult(Unit))
def Device.create_render_pass(device: Device, info: RenderPassCreateInfo) -> IO(VkResult(RenderPass))
def Device.destroy_render_pass(device: Device, pass: RenderPass) -> IO(VkResult(Unit))
def Device.create_framebuffer(device: Device, info: FramebufferCreateInfo) -> IO(VkResult(Framebuffer))
def Device.destroy_framebuffer(device: Device, framebuffer: Framebuffer) -> IO(VkResult(Unit))
def CommandBuffer.pipeline_barrier(command: CommandBuffer, src_stage: U32,
	dst_stage: U32, memory: List<MemoryBarrier>, buffers: List<BufferMemoryBarrier>,
	images: List<ImageMemoryBarrier>) -> IO(VkResult(Unit))
def CommandBuffer.clear_color_image(command: CommandBuffer, image: Image,
	layout: U32, value: ClearColor, ranges: List<ImageSubresourceRange>) -> IO(VkResult(Unit))
def CommandBuffer.clear_depth_image(command: CommandBuffer, image: Image,
	layout: U32, depth: F32, ranges: List<ImageSubresourceRange>) -> IO(VkResult(Unit))
def CommandBuffer.copy_buffer_to_image(command: CommandBuffer, src: Buffer,
	dst: Image, layout: U32, regions: List<BufferImageCopy>) -> IO(VkResult(Unit))
def CommandBuffer.copy_image_to_buffer(command: CommandBuffer, src: Image,
	layout: U32, dst: Buffer, regions: List<BufferImageCopy>) -> IO(VkResult(Unit))
def CommandBuffer.begin_render_pass(command: CommandBuffer, framebuffer: Framebuffer,
	area: RenderArea, clears: List<ClearValue>) -> IO(VkResult(Unit))
def CommandBuffer.end_render_pass(command: CommandBuffer) -> IO(VkResult(Unit))
```

Private-to-the-implementation raw effects use these result adapters. Bend currently has no actual private module visibility, so raw names are documented as transport helpers, never an alternate operation policy.

```python
def ImageFormatWords() -> Type:
	U32 & (U32 & (U32 & (U32 & (U32 & (U32 & (U32 & U32))))))
def Instance.image_format_properties_raw(instance: Instance,
	physical: PhysicalDevice, query: ImageFormatQuery) -> IO(VkResult(ImageFormatWords()))
def Device.image_requirements_raw(device: Device, image: Image) ->
	IO(VkResult(((U32 & U32) & ((U32 & U32) & U32))))
```

`ImageFormatWords` order is max width, height, depth, mips, layers, sample mask, then max-resource-size low and high limbs. Pure adapters reconstruct `W.U64`. The existing buffer requirements raw result shape is reused. No imported U64 constructor CID is referenced in C.

Extend `PhysicalDeviceLimits` and its existing raw-limb adapter with `buffer_image_granularity: W.U64` and `max_framebuffer_layers: U32`. The selected `VkQueueFamilyProperties`, including `minImageTransferGranularity`, is stored in the existing device context. The existing queue-family query shape and `Core.find_queue_family` remain sufficient for selecting graphics in examples. No duplicate public queue-selection API is added.

Color clears accept ordinary F32 values in RGBA component order. The supported normalized and sRGB formats use the float member of `VkClearColorValue`. No packed UI color policy or channel-swizzle constructor is introduced. Reject nonfinite components. Normalized conversion and sRGB encoding follow Vulkan. Depth clears reject nonfinite values and values outside [0,1]. The public depth-only operation maps to `vkCmdClearDepthStencilImage` with stencil zero and DEPTH ranges. See the Khronos [clear-value semantics](https://docs.vulkan.org/spec/latest/chapters/clears.html#clears-values).

The caller-facing pure span helper lives in `src/core.bend`, which cannot import Vulkan.bend because Vulkan already imports Core. It therefore accepts scalar dimensions. Examples use it to size readback buffers and validate expected row locations. Native checks independently enforce the foreign boundary. A differential probe compares both against literal cases, so a pure proof never masquerades as a proof of C.

```python
type BufferImageSpan is Data:
	BufferImageSpan{row_stride: W.U64, layer_stride: W.U64, end: W.U64}
def buffer_image_span(offset: W.U64, texel_bytes: U32,
	width: U32, height: U32, layers: U32, row_length: U32,
	image_height: U32) -> Maybe<BufferImageSpan>
def mip_extent(base: U32, level: U32) -> U32
def subresource_range_valid(base: U32, count: U32, total: U32) -> Bool
```

### Readback dimensions and bytes

Buffer-image transfers preserve the selected format's bytes. `Device.read_memory` returns bytes as U32 values in [0,255]. No image readback effect converts channels, gamma, row orientation, or padding. The example's dimensions are the copied width, height, and layer count, independent of a Bend array's capacity or a staging allocation's size.

| Format | Consecutive bytes per copied texel | Encoding |
|---|---|---|
| R8G8B8A8_UNORM | R, G, B, A | Eight-bit normalized components. No color-space conversion is assigned by the wrapper. |
| B8G8R8A8_UNORM | B, G, R, A | Same normalized values in BGRA byte order. |
| R8G8B8A8_SRGB | R, G, B, A | Stored RGB bytes are sRGB encoded. Alpha is normalized and linear. |
| B8G8R8A8_SRGB | B, G, R, A | Same encoding in BGRA byte order. |
| D16_UNORM | Low byte, high byte on the supported little-endian host | Unsigned normalized depth. |
| D32_SFLOAT | Four bytes of the native IEEE-754 binary32 representation | 0.5 is bytes 00 00 00 3F on the supported little-endian host. |

Texels advance in x first, then increasing image y, then array layer. Logical row zero corresponds to the selected imageOffset.y. The wrapper performs no vertical flip. The example calls y=0 its first, or top, row. Future viewport policy is separate. A tightly packed color region has row stride width times four, while explicit row length and image height determine padded strides. The texel at local x,y,layer has buffer-relative address `O + layer*layer_stride + y*row_stride + x*B`. Only texel bytes are copied. Padding bytes remain untouched.

Copying into or out of an sRGB image transfers stored bytes without gamma conversion. Float clears express linear RGB, which Vulkan encodes for sRGB storage. Endpoint clear colors avoid rounding ambiguity in exact tests. Native float/depth byte probes must confirm the host representation and reject an unsupported endian environment instead of silently using wrong literals.

## Native data shape and one owner per fact

Keep the existing registry key, parent, native handle, and monotonic key allocation. Add four `BvKind` values. Keep the present BvRow scalar fields for existing resources, avoiding an unrelated migration of every row into a new union. Replace row-wide `uses` with command-owned retention. Persistent resources hold typed dependencies only.

```c
typedef struct {
	BvRow **rows;
	uint32_t count;
} BvRetained;

typedef enum { BV_RETAIN_UNCHANGED, BV_RETAIN_REPLACEMENT } BvRetainTag;
typedef struct {
	BvRetainTag tag;
	union { BvRetained replacement; } as;
} BvRetainStage;

typedef struct {
	VkFormat format;
	VkExtent2D extent;
	uint32_t mip_levels, array_layers;
	VkImageUsageFlags usage;
} BvImage;

typedef struct {
	BvRow *image;
	VkImageViewType type;
	VkImageSubresourceRange range;
} BvImageView;

typedef struct {
	VkFormat format;
	VkAttachmentLoadOp load;
	VkAttachmentStoreOp store;
} BvAttachment;

typedef struct {
	uint32_t color_count;
	bool has_depth;
	BvAttachment *attachments;
} BvRenderPass;

typedef struct {
	BvRow *render_pass;
	BvRow **attachments;
	VkExtent2D extent;
	uint32_t layers;
} BvFramebuffer;

typedef enum { BV_OUTSIDE, BV_INSIDE } BvRenderTag;
typedef struct {
	BvRenderTag tag;
	union { struct { BvRow *framebuffer; } inside; } as;
} BvRecording;

typedef struct {
	BvCommandPhase phase;
	union {
		BvRecording recording;
		struct { BvRow *fence; } pending;
		struct { BvRow *fence; } uncertain;
	} state;
	BvRetained retained;
} BvCommand;
```

