Each unit has one code owner across the coupled API, manifest, native, and test files. Each ends with its described verification and a commit. `bend PROOF.bend` runs before every commit. No unit lands generated declarations for unimplemented effects.

1. Establish the ABI and configuration boundary. Add supporting public types, emitted sentinel probe coverage, format traits, image-format query, selected queue granularity caching, physical limit extensions, raw U64 adapters, generator constant groups, and initial pure helpers/laws. Verify exact FORMAT_NOT_SUPPORTED bits through a controlled driver query, all F32 and variant layouts, raw limb roundtrips, generator freshness, proofs, and old suites. Commit the usable capability/ABI boundary.
2. Add image and view resource ownership. Implement image create, requirements, bind, view, destruction, rollback, mixed-allocation interval/granularity policy in both bind directions, and cleanup ordering. Replace existing direct BvUse lists with flat command retention for all existing buffer commands. Verify old alias and active-host behavior, wrong-device/stale/resource lifetime cases, create/bind rollback, allocation faults, proofs, and native sanitizers. Commit resource lifecycle plus the uniform retention foundation.
3. Add image barriers, clear, and copies. Extend the single barrier API and migrate every caller and direct C probe together. Add color/depth clears and both buffer-image directions with checked spans, regions, and queue rules. Verify actual RGBA clear readback, nonuniform padded subrectangle/layer roundtrip, command reuse and bounded rows, integer edge probes, old suites, proofs, generator freshness, and sanitizers. Commit the working offscreen transfer path.
4. Add render-pass and framebuffer execution. Implement typed persistent dependencies, framebuffer expansion into command retention, one-subpass creation, scope state machine, begin/end, load-op clears, compatibility, and cleanup. Verify real color/depth readback, render-area behavior, transitive pending host exclusion, persistent refs, failed reset, all invalid scopes, metadata rollback, proofs, and sanitizers. Commit executable attachment rendering.
