Throughput checkpoint. Grounding precedes code. Independent candidate artifacts may run in parallel. One implementation owner changes this coupled boundary. The IO loop is the sole registry writer. Balanced pure pixel preparation and comparisons may parallelize, while native effects and dependency-changing operations remain sequenced.

## Rationale and accepted tradeoffs

Model the Domain changed two choices. Persistent relationships use fixed typed fields, and render scope lives inside the tagged Recording state. There is no generic adjacency list competing with those fields. See [principle-model-the-domain](/home/aivv/.agents/skills/principle-model-the-domain/SKILL.md).

Boundary Discipline keeps all forgeable handle, ABI, ownership, enum, usage, and range checks at the native effects boundary. Pure arithmetic helpers receive explicit values and return errors as data. See [principle-boundary-discipline](/home/aivv/.agents/skills/principle-boundary-discipline/SKILL.md).

Minimize Reader Load changed active host protection to direct allocation membership in the command's retained set. A maintainer answering why a memory access is rejected reads the existing command association and one set, without tracing framebuffer traversal or synchronized counters. See [principle-minimize-reader-load](/home/aivv/.agents/skills/principle-minimize-reader-load/SKILL.md).

Sequence Work into Verifiable Units separates a usable resource lifecycle, a real transfer result, and executable attachment clears into checked commits. Prove It Works requires the independent literal pixel expectations and actual native artifacts in the acceptance table. See [sequence principle](/home/aivv/.agents/skills/principle-sequence-verifiable-units/SKILL.md) and [verification principle](/home/aivv/.agents/skills/principle-prove-it-works/SKILL.md).

- We accept a larger command retention set in exchange for allocation-free active-host and destruction queries. Set growth occurs before void dispatch and can fail safely.
- We accept a typed expansion case when a new resource kind arrives in exchange for structurally bounded ownership and no recursive safety traversal. Future descriptor sets must similarly freeze dependencies or introduce a different explicit lifetime mechanism.
- We accept whole-allocation host exclusion in exchange for retaining milestone 1's simple and conservative alias guarantee.
- We accept explicit old-layout and initialization responsibility in exchange for no recording-time fiction about execution. Misstated layouts remain a documented caller error beyond the wrapper's static checks.
- We accept stricter image alias and region-envelope policies in exchange for sound checks without guessing optimal image storage. Existing buffer-only aliasing stays usable.
- We accept one-subpass, single-sample, six-format image support in exchange for a verified offscreen and next-stage indexed graphics foundation. Arrays, mip ranges, multiple colors, depth, and raw transfers remain first-class.
- We accept requiring NoClear placeholders in exchange for unambiguous attachment ordering and precise validation. The native boundary hides VkClearValue union representation.

## Synthesis decision

This is candidate 3 for the parent design comparison. Its base is typed persistent ownership plus flat command retention and explicit caller layouts. It rejects generic graph traversal, ownership aggregates, and layout ledgers for the reasons above. No claim is made about other candidates or the parent's final selection.

The red-flag review found no second writer for submission, binding, busy state, or layout. Raw ABI helpers remain a known existing importability limitation of Bend modules. They expose representation adaptation only, not a second lifetime or barrier route. Immutable typed pointers and command retention have different ownership lifetimes and require no synchronized mutation.

## Residual questions to resolve experimentally

1. What exact F32 extraction and nested variant layouts does this installed Bend 2.0.37 emit for mixed clear-value lists and nested ranges? Resolve with emitted sentinel C and direct native assertions before adding marshalling. Do not infer field counts.
2. Does this physical device support D32_SFLOAT with optimal depth-attachment plus transfer-source usage, and which allowed fallback configurations work? Resolve through the configuration query and real pass/readback. Report exact formats exercised.
3. Which accepted image memory types are also host-visible, allowing the actual-driver framebuffer-to-allocation host-busy check? Resolve memory requirements and type queries. Keep deterministic native lifetime probes if the hardware cannot supply that combination.
4. Do the selected queue's actual transfer granularity and format limits permit the planned two-layer padded subrectangle case? Read selected queue properties and query array-layer support, then choose a positive legal test extent. Keep mocked granularity edge cases separately labeled.
5. Do sanitizer and fault-injection runs expose any wrapper allocation that occurs after a void recording dispatch or leaks a partially built attachment/retention owner? Resolve with allocation-site fault enumeration, unchanged-state assertions, and destructor counters.

The first implementation step is the emitted ABI probe and exact configuration-query boundary in unit 1. Its evidence fixes native decoding before any new GPU command is recorded.
