There are seventeen new generated effects. The two typed result adapters are ordinary Bend defs. `begin_render_pass` obtains its exact render-pass handle from the framebuffer. A redundant caller-supplied render-pass argument would create a compatibility decision at every begin. Lists are consumed normally. No new effect takes an affine array. Existing packed uploads continue to return the same array owner on every native and JavaScript outcome.

### Supported creation profile

The public shape can describe later growth, but M2 accepts the following profile. Unsupported wrapper configurations return BV_ARGUMENT before Vulkan creation. A valid queried configuration rejected by the driver returns its exact Vulkan result.

| Decision | M2 behavior |
| --- | --- |
| Image type and tiling | 2D, optimal, depth 1. No direct image mapping or linear-image row-layout API. |
| Samples | Exactly SAMPLE_COUNT_1. No resolve or multisample attachment path. |
| Mips and arrays | Positive counts within configuration limits. Mips no greater than `1 + floor(log2(max(width,height)))`. Copies select one mip and any positive layer interval. Barriers and clears accept explicit finite ranges across mips and layers. |
| Sharing and initial layout | Exclusive selected queue family. Creation uses UNDEFINED. No PREINITIALIZED, queue transfers, concurrent sharing, external memory, sparse binding, or extension chains. |
| Image flags | Creation accepts flags 0. No mutable format or cube-compatible image. |
| Usages | Nonempty subset of TRANSFER_SRC, TRANSFER_DST, SAMPLED, COLOR_ATTACHMENT, DEPTH_STENCIL_ATTACHMENT. Color/depth usage must agree with the format class. No transient or lazily allocated images, storage, or input attachments in M2. |
| Views | 2D for a single layer, or 2D_ARRAY for a positive layer range. Exact image format, identity component mapping, nonempty bounded mip/layer range. No cube, 1D, 3D, reinterpretation, or swizzle. A view needs a view-eligible usage, here sampled or attachment usage. |
| Framebuffers | One layer, positive width/height within device limits. One mip and one layer per attachment view, view type 2D. Multiple color attachments up to the selected physical limit and optional depth/stencil. At least one attachment. |
| Image aliasing | Different image allocations may share one DeviceMemory only through nonoverlapping requirement intervals. Overlap involving an image rejects at either image or buffer binding, even if the caller promises disjoint execution. Existing buffer-to-buffer aliases remain supported. |

The single native format descriptor table is authoritative for the accepted formats, aspects, numeric class, storage bytes, and buffer-copy element size. Generate Vulkan enumerants from the existing registry provenance. The descriptor table represents wrapper policy and is handwritten once, beside image marshalling. Do not duplicate its list in several switches.

| Accepted formats | Aspects | Bytes per copied aspect element |
| --- | --- | --- |
| R8G8B8A8_UNORM, R8G8B8A8_SRGB | COLOR | 4 |
| B8G8R8A8_UNORM, B8G8R8A8_SRGB | COLOR | 4 |
| D16_UNORM | DEPTH | 2 |
| D32_SFLOAT | DEPTH | 4 |
| D24_UNORM_S8_UINT | DEPTH and STENCIL | 4 for DEPTH, 1 for STENCIL |
| D32_SFLOAT_S8_UINT | DEPTH and STENCIL | 4 for DEPTH, 1 for STENCIL |

All accepted formats have a one by one by one block extent. Image storage sizes for logical limit calculations are 4 bytes for D24/S8 and 8 bytes for D32/S8. Those sizes do not replace `vkGetImageMemoryRequirements`. Integer-color, compressed, packed-color, and multi-planar formats reject. This keeps float clears honest. It supports ordinary M3 color and depth targets, and later sampled 2D arrays, without a universal image claim.

